    "body": "### Problem\n\nthe documentation (:help vim.lsp) says: \n- `single_file_support` is assumed by default. Can be disabled by specifying\n  `workspace_required=false` (see |vim.lsp.ClientConfig|).\n\nwhereas it appears that setting workspace_required to false actually makes single files not supported.\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n:help vim.lsp\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nthe documentation (:help vim.lsp) should say: \n- `single_file_support` is assumed by default. Can be disabled by specifying\n  `workspace_required=true` (see |vim.lsp.ClientConfig|).\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.12.4\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nwindows 10\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nneovide\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nidk\n\n### Installation\n\nscoop",
